      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1927 the area was split between Michigan and Indiana and developed simultaneously by the Long Beach Development Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://michianavillage.org/michiana-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Michigan side incorporated as Michiana Village in 1946, the day the village officially became a municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://michianavillage.org/michiana-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A tree known as the Signal Oak once marked the corner of Michiana Drive and Ponchartrain Trail, and an amphitheater was built around it for prospective buyers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
